      "widgets_values": [
        2,
        "Title: Polar Bear Doing Yoga on Mat Wellness Fitness Humor Meditation\n\nKeywords: polar bear, yoga, yoga mat, meditation, wellness humor, fitness funny, yoga class, downward dog, yoga pose, mindfulness, zen, funny animal, gym humor, pilates, athleisure, workout humor, yoga studio, flexibility, stretching, self care, wellness lifestyle, hot yoga irony, animal yoga, relaxation, balance, peaceful, namaste humor\n\n===\n\nPhotorealistic humorous vertical image of a large polar bear performing a yoga pose on a premium yoga mat in a clean, modern yoga studio. The polar bear is attempting a seated meditation pose or gentle stretch, sitting upright with eyes peacefully closed and paws resting on its knees in a meditation mudra. Its thick white fur contrasts beautifully with the colorful yoga mat beneath it.\n\nThe polar bear wears a simple athletic headband or perhaps has a small towel draped around its neck, suggesting it takes its practice seriously. Its expression is one of complete zen and tranquility, as if it has achieved enlightenment despite being an Arctic animal in a warm yoga studio.\n\nThe yoga studio setting is bright, airy, and aspirational with natural light streaming through large windows, light wood floors, and minimalist decor. Perhaps other yoga mats are visible in the background, suggesting a class setting. Plants, mirrors, and clean white walls complete the wellness aesthetic.\n\nThe yoga mat is high-quality looking, perhaps in a rich jewel tone or earthy color that complements the polar bear's white fur. The mat should look like a premium brand without showing any actual logos.\n\nVertical composition places the polar bear centered on the yoga mat, studio environment visible around and behind. Bright, clean lighting. Space at top of frame for text overlay. The overall aesthetic should feel like a premium yoga studio Instagram post, but starring a polar bear.\n\nSuitable for fitness brand humor, yoga studio marketing, wellness content, social media templates, mindfulness apps, gym promotional content, and lifestyle blog imagery.\n\nNegative: blurry, low quality, distorted, watermark, text, logo, cartoon style, illustration, aggressive bear pose, melting or sad imagery, dark gym, dirty environment, obvious CGI, sweaty gross aesthetic, cramped space, uncomfortable expression",
